  "assumptions": [
    "SPI1 APB2=72MHz /8 and SPI2 APB1=36MHz /4 both produce 9MHz; external header switches SPI1 to /128=562.5kHz (budgeted conservatively at 500kHz).",
    "One RX plus one TX W5500 128-byte payload per 8ms =128kbit/s per direction; 64 bytes transaction/control overhead reserved per service.",
    "CAN arrival upper estimates assume 10% offered load, full 8-byte Classical frames >=111 wire bits; FD frames 64 bytes >=30/500k+512/2M seconds; include rounding upward.",
    "CAN clients each drain one frame per 1ms. Engineering dossier budgets eight RX/TX/TEF slots per controller with RX and TEF timestamps; total Classical384 bytes/FD1280 bytes within2KB. Driver setup, CRC/ECC initialization and timing remain unverified.",
    "No simultaneous SPI DMA; three USART TX/RX DMA pairs occupy channels2-7. I2C1 interrupts; both SPIs bounded polling with per-client clock switching and CS discipline.",
    "Wire-time includes a 20us chosen overhead per job, not measured MCU WCET. Complete CPU/scheduler/USB/serial/I2C throughput remains unknown.",
    "Reserve currents and 80% efficiency are engineering estimates, not maximum manufacturer guarantees. CAN VIO is separately reserved at2mA on3V3; direct CAN VDD remains on5V.",
    "External 5V only; VBUS divider/backfeed circuit, USB-C CC resistors, protection, crystal/passives/BOM/assets and silicon-specific errata handling remain circuit-review dependencies."
  ]
